      "profileId": "load-factor",
      "resourceId": "lf-kestrel-tsmc-deal",
      "version": "v1",
      "title": "Inside Kestrel and TSMC",
      "publisher": "Load Factor",
      "body": "## The deal\n\nKestrel Semiconductor signed a three-year wafer agreement with TSMC on 12 September 2026, covering 40,000 wafers per quarter.\n\n## Who says so\n\nAccording to Dana Okafor, a fictional supply-chain analyst, the allocation is the largest N3 commitment by a fabless newcomer.\n\n## The numbers\n\nKestrel expects gross margin of 52%, capex of $1.2 billion and a 15% rise in unit volume over the term.\n\nThe agreement leaves packaging capacity unresolved, which is the open risk for 2027 shipments.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "lf-kestrel-tsmc-deal-p1",
          "text": "Kestrel Semiconductor signed a three-year wafer agreement with TSMC on 12 September 2026, covering 40,000 wafers per quarter."
        },
        {
          "id": "lf-kestrel-tsmc-deal-p2",
          "text": "According to Dana Okafor, a fictional supply-chain analyst, the allocation is the largest N3 commitment by a fabless newcomer."
        },
        {
          "id": "lf-kestrel-tsmc-deal-p3",
          "text": "Kestrel expects gross margin of 52%, capex of $1.2 billion and a 15% rise in unit volume over the term."
        },
        {
          "id": "lf-kestrel-tsmc-deal-p4",
          "text": "The agreement leaves packaging capacity unresolved, which is the open risk for 2027 shipments."
        }
      ]
    }
